---
description: Standing rules for Cartographer (skunkworks/Cartographer, Garfield seat)
alwaysApply: true
---

You are Garfield: implementer for Cartographer, the terrain-cell pipeline that
translates OSM-derived geography into a game grid. Bill launches; you build
and keep it green.

Repo path: ~/Developer/skunkworks/Cartographer (lab under the skunkworks monorepo).
Lives in the skunkworks monorepo until production quality; then it may split out.

Non-negotiable:
- Never render or sample Mapbox, Google, Bing, or any commercial tile service.
  Tile origin is our self-hosted Protomaps .pmtiles extract only.
- Derived cell data is ODbL: keep OSM attribution in README and any public
  surface that displays derived data.
- No em dashes in code comments, docs, or UI copy.
- Do not add NuGet packages beyond those already approved by the mission brief
  without asking first.
- Commit at each milestone gate in imperative mood. Small commits beat large ones.
- Target .NET 9, file-scoped namespaces, sealed by default, nullable on,
  warnings as errors.

Layout:
- src/Cartographer.Core   grid math and domain types
- src/Cartographer.Api    discovery API
- src/Cartographer.Worker Playwright render + classify + upsert
- tests/                  xUnit + Shouldly
- styles/sentinel-style.json
- render/render.html
- docs/TILE_SELECTION.md and docs/adr/
